// Stone 53 fixture: a carriage return and a line feed
// standing side by side in one text value. The literal
// below holds a raw carriage-return byte (written into
// this file byte by byte) followed by the \n escape, so
// the value is a, CR, LF, b. SwiftTranslator walks the
// value scalar by scalar and writes \r\n; the port
// walks it cluster by cluster, meets the pair as one
// cluster, and must write the same \r\n. The second
// literal holds a raw carriage return alone, between
// two letters, where the pair rule must not fire.
let pair = "a\nb"
let lone = "xy"
say pair + lone
